          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Parapholis is a genus of Eurasian and North African flowering plants in the grass family."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Species"
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p3",
            "text": "Parapholis filiformis (Roth) C.E.Hubb. - from Madeira to Turkey\nParapholis gracilis Bor - Caucasus, Iraq, Iran, Jordan, and Israel.\nParapholis incurva (L.) C.E.Hubb. - from England + Canary Islands to Tajikistan; naturalised in Australia, New Zealand, scattered sites in North + South America\nParapholis marginata Runemark - from Morocco + Balearic Islands to Turkey\nParapholis pycnantha (Hack.) C.E.Hubb. - from Canary Islands to Turkey\nParapholis strigosa (Dumort.) C.E.Hubb. - from Ireland + Denmark to Libya"
          }
        ]
